--
N5008 [expr.new]/1 + [temp.variadic]/5,7: a new-initializer's expression
list is a pack-expansion context; with an EMPTY pack `::new((void *)p)
U(forward<Args>(args)...)' is `::new((void *)p) U()' (value-initialization,
[dcl.init.general]/9).  For a namespace-scope function template
(std::construct_at) this works since round 162
(cpp20_construct_at_empty_pack_placement_new); for a MEMBER function
template of a class template -- libc++'s `allocator<T>::construct(U *,
Args &&...)' -- the instance with no arguments is dropped silently (no
diagnostic), so every libc++ C++11 vector/list push_back reads the new
element as nondet (audit residue item 5, round 162).  The call with
arguments converts.
